---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Mechanics Quick Reference | Free SUVAT, Forces, Energy"
  description="Complete mechanics quick reference with SUVAT equations, forces, and energy formulas. Free download for physics and engineering students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Mechanics<br><span>Quick Reference</span></h1>
    <p>SUVAT equations, forces, and energy formulas. From kinematics to work-energy theorem.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>SUVAT Equations</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Equations of Motion</h3>
        <pre><code>v = u + at
s = ut + ½at²
v² = u² + 2as
s = ½(u + v)t
s = vt - ½at²</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Forces</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Newton's Laws</h3>
        <pre><code>F = ma (2nd law)
F₁₂ = -F₂₁ (3rd law)
Weight: W = mg
Friction: F ≤ μR</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Momentum</h3>
        <pre><code>p = mv
Impulse: J = FΔt = Δp
Conservation: m₁u₁ + m₂u₂ = m₁v₁ + m₂v₂</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Energy</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Energy Types</h3>
        <pre><code>KE = ½mv²
PE (gravitational) = mgh
PE (elastic) = ½kx²
Work = Fd cos θ</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Power</h3>
        <pre><code>P = W/t
P = Fv
P = ΔE/Δt</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Circular Motion</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Formulas</h3>
        <pre><code>a = v²/r (centripetal)
F = mv²/r (centripetal)
ω = 2πf = 2π/T
v = ωr</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
